+WHAT CLARK'S 15.4 HAD THAT WE DON'T (YET)
+â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€â”€
+
+  1. Time/Byte Bank PSA installer in PCBSM
+     Clark's PCBSM had "Time/Byte Bank Support" + "PCBBANK" as a
+     menu entry.  Our PPL tokens (GETBANKBAL/SETBANKBAL) are in
+     PPLC but the PCBSM installer and timebank_psa_t struct aren't
+     landed.  The PPL dispatch currently safe-no-ops (v0.029 fix).
+
+  2. "Edit User Record (Personal Form)"
+     Clark had a dedicated form view in PCBSM's user editor with
+     field-aligned labels (trailing-space-padded).  Our PCBSM has
+     a working but simpler "Edit Personal Info" menu entry.
+
+  3. MKPCBTXT 15.4 format support
+     Clark's MKPCBTXT knows about 15.3 AND 15.4 text file versions.
+     Ours only handles 15.3.
+
+  4. CHAT @X color codes + action commands (WHATSNEW #3)
+     Not touched.  Would require changes to CHAT.C.
+
+  5. File flagging by number (WHATSNEW #6)
+     Not verified or implemented.
+
+  6. PPL enhanced security algorithm (WHATSNEW #5)
+     PPE encryption/anti-busting layer.  Not reverse-engineered.
+
+  All six are RE-able from Clark's 15.4b binaries whenever there's
+  appetite.  The build machinery is stable and proven.
